Cell["\<\
As seen in this image, CTAB consists of a long hydrocarbon chain with a \
positively charged nitrogen head-group. Due to the partial negative charge on \
the oxygen atoms, water is highly polar and primarily interacts with the \
positively charged nitrogen rather than the bromide. The simplicity of the \
nitrogen in comparison in CTAB means that the Lennard-Jones depth and \
size-proxy for it is available. The ubiquitousness of water means that its \
depth and size proxy are also recorded (Water Models, n.dn).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9606320561966724`*^9, 3.960632060429188*^9}, {
   3.9606321017114677`*^9, 3.960632106891081*^9}, {3.9606442291461563`*^9, 
   3.960644259771906*^9}, {3.9606508050989704`*^9, 3.960650835899929*^9}, 
   3.9607357675875607`*^9, {3.960885288839897*^9, 3.9608852916236744`*^9}, {
   3.960891916298502*^9, 3.9608919188154755`*^9}, {3.9611154183739157`*^9, 
   3.96111551022563*^9}, {3.961139151996695*^9, 3.961139153641316*^9}, {
   3.961171225178254*^9, 
   3.961171233415278*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"dce42070-4c88-cb46-95dc-\
72bbdd951680"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\nHere, the  Lennard-Jones depths and size proxies of each individual \
components of CTAB, a cationic surfactant, are recorded, as well as for \
Water. As the positive head of the surfactant, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["N", "4"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ad29a465-9544-6e45-bfb4-739cc5e45702"],
 " ion is the group that bonds with the anionic poles of the water molecule. \
Thus, when looking at the epsilon and sigma values for CTAB-water \
interactions, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["N", "4"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "efc8939b-1635-684e-ba0e-f650873c86af"],
 " will be approximated to represent the sigma and epsilon of CTAB."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.960299533974106*^9, 3.960299675900404*^9}, {
   3.9602997097132015`*^9, 3.9602997844652863`*^9}, {3.9602998146780586`*^9, 
   3.960299835863186*^9}, 3.9606320526039524`*^9, {3.960891873995325*^9, 
   3.9608919124833946`*^9}, {3.961028894105556*^9, 3.9610288999430656`*^9}, {
   3.9610289382779903`*^9, 3.96102893933634*^9}, {3.961030098065675*^9, 
   3.961030107944621*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c46dc026-7c26-eb4f-b33b-\
fe8555830214"],

Cell["\<\
The Lennard-Jones depth and size-proxies (epsilon and sigma, respectively) \
are defined as variables with already known values.\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9610287609199963`*^9, 3.961028803286022*^9}, {
  3.9610289432208357`*^9, 
  3.961028947923317*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9191c3b4-ec22-e742-b39d-\
8a86358482e9"],

