      RowBox[{"t", ",", 
       RowBox[{"condensateFcn", "[", 
        RowBox[{"radialDistance", "[", "t", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", "0.1", ",", "40", ",", "0.01"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tFirst", "=", 
   RowBox[{"First", "@", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
      RowBox[{"data", ",", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Last", "[", "#", "]"}], "==", "1"}], "&"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", "tFirst"}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.960631083151285*^9, 3.960631107399481*^9}, 
   3.961025669113448*^9, {3.961111845712309*^9, 3.9611118484461117`*^9}, {
   3.961162836495473*^9, 3.9611628732796907`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1101]:=",ExpressionUUID->"651e80f2-b470-044a-bd82-083cfb53aada"],

Cell[BoxData["0.77`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.961162873574946*^9, 3.961163016096903*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1103]=",ExpressionUUID->"c112753f-8e60-354f-ada7-f504ba200b5c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
As seen in this graph and output, the minimum threshold for condensation is \
0.360nm. To evaluate whether this is a realistic estimate, the \
\[OpenCurlyQuote]bond\[CloseCurlyQuote] length of the Nitrogen cation and \
partial-negative Oxygen must be compared to it. As the two molecules will be \
held together via an IMF rather than a covalent bond, the minimum threshold \
must be within twice the sum of the combined Van der Waals of Nitrogen and \
Oxygen.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9608874425383186`*^9, 3.960887578704754*^9}, {
   3.9610249130471287`*^9, 3.961024913268649*^9}, {3.9610253303995523`*^9, 
   3.9610253886043787`*^9}, 
   3.961163017219095*^9},ExpressionUUID->"e49c35cf-f27a-8944-bce2-\
4f821c569d45"],

Cell["\<\
The Van der Waals radius of nitrogen and oxygen are fetched from the \
ElementData dataset and then added together.\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.961025397914524*^9, 
  3.961025418292069*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ee680617-f886-8948-b0e8-\
e835d8cda016"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"vdwN", "=", 
   RowBox[{"ElementData", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Nitrogen\>\"", ",", "\"\<VanDerWaalsRadius\>\""}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"vdwO", "=", 
    RowBox[{"ElementData", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Oxygen\>\"", ",", "\"\<VanDerWaalsRadius\>\""}], "]"}]}], 
   ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"vdwNnm", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Quantity", "[", 
    RowBox[{"vdwN", ",", "\"\<Nanometers\>\""}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"vdwOnm", "=", 
    RowBox[{"Quantity", "[", 
     RowBox[{"vdwO", ",", "\"\<Nanometers\>\""}], "]"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"sumRadius", " ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"vdwNnm", " ", "+", " ", "vdwOnm"}]}], ";"}], 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "sumRadius"}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9608876281546993`*^9, {3.960887722097826*^9, 3.960887732957224*^9}, {
   3.960887798924753*^9, 3.960887827016363*^9}, {3.9608878663912086`*^9, 
   3.960887880396673*^9}, {3.9608879113343945`*^9, 3.9608879448144817`*^9}, {
   3.9608879777841244`*^9, 3.9608881044160748`*^9}, 
   3.9611636989172907`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"03e25c3e-71be-c749-89dc-\
ae923ea43833"],

Cell["\<\
As 0.466 is within 2x the value of the combined radii, 0.307nm, it is safe to \
assume that Intermolecular Forces can hold the surfactant molecule to the \
water vapor molecule, thus making this threshold function realistic.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9606316595365925`*^9, 3.960631671741377*^9}, {
  3.9608871275670586`*^9, 3.960887169806055*^9}, {3.96102568967907*^9, 
  3.9610256923883*^9}, {3.961028375228587*^9, 3.96102841604078*^9}, {
  3.961029542424473*^9, 3.961029546485345*^9}, {3.961031910425256*^9, 
  3.961031978458877*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ea59015a-b3b7-a24a-868c-\
72c02eb66105"],

Cell["\<\
Thus, by using rudimentary estimates of the Lennard-Jones depth and \
size-proxy of a known surfactant, CTAB, it was possible to model its \
interaction with a water-vapor via the Lennard-Jones potential. It was found \
that the critical radius that could lead to condensation was 0.307nm. Though \
this is useful information, very little is told to us about how relevant it \
is in the context of cloud seeding without comparing it to a non-seeded \
environment where there are only water molecules. Though it is true that \
Aerosol Particles (AP) are necessary to produce clouds, they have miniscule \
impacts on the condensation of water vapor and its process to become heavy \
enough to precipitate.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.961028627961651*^9, 3.961028642728211*^9}, {
  3.961029679979992*^9, 
  3.961029879175828*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"676da540-f9c8-374a-919f-\
77025a956543"],

Cell["\<\
To compare how effective seeded CTAB is to a non-seeded environment, the \
minimum threshold for condensation can be calculated assuming there are only \
water-water interactions by calculating the critical radius where the \
size-proxy is that of solely water.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.961031755574164*^9, 
  3.9610318136689053`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d45ebd8b-c75a-3645-9b65-\
2ae99e599d20"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"0.3166", "*", 
  RowBox[{"2", "^", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "6"}], ")"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.961031817528652*^9, 3.96103184199041*^9}, {
  3.961031987162848*^9, 3.961031999317767*^9}, {3.961032604162521*^9, 
  3.961032605119308*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[1100]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d39d8270-48f4-0e4f-a244-0acc06d5790e"],

Cell[BoxData["0.3553714844947475`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9611617973205357`*^9, 3.961162995438101*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[1100]=",ExpressionUUID->"43232a38-1491-554b-857e-47968b55e5b5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The water-CTAB critical radius is around 150% that of the water-water \
critical radius. The difference means that water molecules can experience \
condensation with a surfactant molecule at larger distances than they can \
with another water molecule, thus meaning that they experience stronger \
attractive forces.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.96103201281966*^9, 3.961032150171754*^9}, {
  3.961032187308569*^9, 
  3.961032247958709*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f32b3deb-770d-034a-b37a-\
5b5f9ae1a8b7"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Potential Energy Scan for Lennard-Jones Parameters", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9610113059772*^9, 3.96101130982718*^9}, {
  3.961032306992311*^9, 
  3.9610323156073914`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b9a176c7-7aed-ca44-b15d-\
eff19d1a67d6"],

Cell["\<\
What is very important to note about the previous example was that the \
epsilon and sigma values that were used for CTAB were estimates, based off \
Nitrogen-Nitrogen interactions. Nitrogen was the positively charged ion in \
CTAB, and due to the lack of data availability, it was considered in \
isolation with water. As electrons from different atoms will influence this \
interaction, to have a better estimate, the Schrodinger\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
Equation must be modeled through the Wolfram Quantum Chemistry Paclets. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.960914199008635*^9, 3.960914339176675*^9}, {
  3.960971190797332*^9, 3.960971256589287*^9}, {3.9609712907113028`*^9, 
  3.960971325854066*^9}, {3.9610347295847588`*^9, 3.961034730911311*^9}, {
  3.96113968833992*^9, 
  3.961139692239271*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fa65b9cf-b597-fd4c-a74c-\
89cef9e4f605"],

Cell["\<\
The Paclet must be installed to the system via PacletInstall.\
\>", "CodeText",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.961034751908291*^9, {3.961163703855776*^9, 
   3.961163707451082*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6c24d652-1dfc-cc4d-b960-\
c908ac521661"],

