Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[49]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9381ccbf-be9d-cc4a-803d-847ed1e4159b"],

Cell["\<\
With the creation of this new molecule and molecule bond, the geometry must \
once again be optimized. When a molecule is created, a \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]guess\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] geometry is returned-- \
and this geometry is often not the most optimal structure. The optimal \
structure is naturally preferred by the molecule as it is the true \
equilibrium structure and the energy minimum on the potential energy surface. \
As the PotentialEnergyScan holds all other coordinates fixed , beginning at \
an unrelaxed geometry means that bond lengths and angles will be wrong. Thus, \
before completing this step, the geometry of not only CTAB but CTAB\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s interaction with water must be optimized.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9609736703879023`*^9, 3.960973701748231*^9}, {
  3.960980337924686*^9, 
  3.960980338545568*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f5a09bcb-2602-f246-bf2d-\
c00a80e8d2b8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData["interaction"], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[50]:=",ExpressionUUID->"830cce20-6290-5b4d-ba41-96d81f46c34b"],

