Cell["\<\
As seen in a previous section, the minimum distance for condensation is \
calculated by taking the derivative of the Lennard-Jones equation, or rather \
multiplying the size-proxy by the sixth-root of 2. These calculations show a \
distance of 0.529 nm. As already discussed, the combined Van der Waals radius \
of Nitrogen and Oxygen is approximately 0.307nm. As the distance of 0.529 is \
within 1 - 2x that value, it is logical that a Van der Waals force can form \
between the surfactant and the water molecule, leading to condensation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.961015255047057*^9, 3.961015320192607*^9}, {
  3.96101535649506*^9, 3.9610153865605507`*^9}, {3.961015515876532*^9, 
  3.961015603477507*^9}, {3.961015819477862*^9, 3.961015821244801*^9}, {
  3.9610230558077383`*^9, 
  3.961023066587384*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"138a7595-50bf-4244-9024-\
1f0c30005b0c"],

