Cell["\<\
As shown in the 3D plot, the surfactant molecule contains a total of eight \
oxygen atoms. To determine the optimized geometry, a hydrogen atom must be \
individually bonded to each of these oxygen sites, and the corresponding \
complex energy for each configuration will be recorded. The configuration \
with the lowest complex energy represents the most favorable bonding site. \
Once the optimal geometry is identified, a potential energy scan can be \
performed and the results fit to the Lennard-Jones equation, as was \
previously done for CTAB.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.961145258471953*^9, 3.961145360823886*^9}, {
  3.961145395614688*^9, 
  3.961145396941229*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"459216d5-6173-5941-9544-\
308a468b0a81"],

